WEBVTT

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:33.172
Often, most times wearing
translation headphones,

00:01:33.172 --> 00:01:35.591
speaking into a thin microphone.

00:01:36.676 --> 00:01:39.929
The judge, for every single case,
would, in essence,

00:01:39.971 --> 00:01:41.639
read the very same instructions.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:45.810
Describing the process,
what would come next,

00:01:45.852 --> 00:01:47.478
what to expect.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:49.981
He made sure that

00:01:50.022 --> 00:01:54.443
if the immigrants had any questions,
they were answered,

00:01:54.443 --> 00:01:57.905
but they were also able to explain
their side of the case.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:02.034
The attorney with Immigration
and Customs Enforcement,